Title: Login Button Not Visible on Mobile Devices

Environment:

- Browser: (e.g., Google Chrome, Firefox, Safari)

- Operating System: (e.g., Android, iOS, Windows)

- Device Type: Mobile (e.g., iPhone, Android Phone)

- App Version: If it is available

- URL: https://www.saucedemo.com/

Severity: High (Affects core functionality)

Priority: P1 (Critical – blocks users from logging in on mobile)

Description: The 'Login' button is not visible when accessing the Swag Labs (saucedemo.com) site on mobile devices. This issue prevents users from logging in, making it critical for mobile users.

Steps to Reproduce:

1. Open a mobile browser (e.g., Safari or Chrome) on your device.

2. Navigate to https://www.saucedemo.com/.

3. Input a valid username in the "Username" field.

4. Input a valid password in the "Password" field.

5. Observe the login page layout.

6. The 'Login' button will not be visible on the screen.

Expected Result: The 'Login' button should be visible and accessible for users to click after entering the username and password fields on mobile devices.

Actual Result: The 'Login' button is not visible on mobile devices, preventing users from logging in.

Screenshots/Video: Here we should attach screenshots or screen recordings showing the issue if available

Impact:

- Users on mobile devices are unable to log in to their accounts, affecting user experience and business operations.

- Mobile users are unable to access the site fully, leading to frustration and potential loss of users.

Additional Information:

- This issue only occurs on mobile devices; it works as expected on desktop devices.

- Possible causes may include CSS styling issues, viewport or media query errors, or elements being hidden due to responsive design breakpoints.

Steps for Fix/Next Steps:

- Investigate the CSS for mobile breakpoints and ensure the 'Login' button is visible on smaller screens.

- Check for any hidden elements or media query conditions that could affect the visibility of the button.

